arch=x86
vmlinux_btf=7.0 kernel BTF dump (bpftool btf dump file /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux format c, Ubuntu 24.04.5, 7.0.0-42-generic)
clang=Ubuntu clang version 18.1.3 (1ubuntu1)
load_verified=bpftool prog loadall, Ubuntu x86_64 7.0.0-42-generic, all 15 programs pinned
  (kprobe__mnt_want_write_file is the new one) and wire_map created. NOT re-run
  on the legacy matrix this object's predecessor was checked against: AlmaLinux
  8.10 (4.18.0-553), CentOS Linux 8.5 (4.18.0-348), Amazon Linux 2 (5.10),
  Amazon Linux 2023 (6.1), Ubuntu 20.04 (5.15 HWE), openSUSE Leap 16.0 (6.12).
notes=rebuilt for RT_ABI_MAJOR 2 (variable-length record, doc 34 F4) plus the
  mnt_want_write_file probe and the ATTR_FILE mount override (F1) and the
  admission hoisting (F8). 15 programs and 9 program sections, against the 14
  and 8 of the object it replaces; one map more (wire_map, a per-CPU scratch of
  one rt_file_event_wire). Same host, kernel and clang as the predecessor, so
  the only inputs that changed are the two files the digest covers.
